>>
Rule 1 (input must be real-valued; complex not supported)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 2 (when out is provided, its dtype must match input to avoid dtype mismatch)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (when out is provided, its shape must match input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 4 (when out is provided, both input and out must be real-valued)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 7 (explicitly prevent Float-vs-Double mismatch when input is Double)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 8 then dtype_(v_2) = 8
